<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Hanau-Lichtenberg</h1><p class="st-meta">1480 CE – 1736 CE · capital Buchsweiler</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A county straddling the Rhine in northern Alsace and Baden, formed when a branch of the counts of Hanau inherited half of Lichtenberg in 1480.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1458 the County of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-hanau-munzenberg">Hanau</a> was divided, and Philip I the Younger received a share. In 1480 his line inherited half of the lordship of Lichtenberg in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a> through marriage, forming the County of Hanau-Lichtenberg, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bouxwiller">Buchsweiler</a> (Bouxwiller) as its capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The counts ruled scattered lands on both banks of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, including the Hanauerland around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kehl">Kehl</a>. They introduced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Lutheran Reformation</a> in the 1540s and ran a well-ordered small state. In 1642 they inherited the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-hanau-munzenberg">County of Hanau-Münzenberg</a>. From 1680 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reunions">Reunions</a> placed the Alsatian lands under French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>, though the counts kept their estates and revenues.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When the last count, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-reinhard-iii-of-hanau">Johann Reinhard III</a>, died in 1736, Hanau-Lichtenberg passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/landgraviate-of-hesse-darmstadt">Landgraviate of Hesse-Darmstadt</a>. The French Revolution swept away its Alsatian lordship, and in 1803 the lands east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="county, 1480 CE – 1736 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">county</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.15%;width:5.09%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1480 CE – 1736 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Buchsweiler</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Philip I the Younger, Johann Reinhard III</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Alsatian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a>, <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hanau-Lichtenberg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1608&amp;focus=county-of-hanau-lichtenberg" aria-label="County of Hanau-Lichtenberg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4853 473 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County of Hanau-Lichtenberg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5173 729L5204 690M5173 729L5198 698"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5204 690h0M5198 698h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5173 729h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5173 729h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1608&amp;focus=county-of-hanau-lichtenberg">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
